  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A network of four resistances is connected to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> battery, as shown in figure. The magnitude of voltage difference between the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is __________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0067_a43b3b6546ce.png\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 303px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The resistance in each branch is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. They are in parallel. So, net resistance is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p>The total current flowing through the loop,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Thus, through each branch the current is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence, the voltage difference across the points is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}